# Wave W17-R (Route 124 Trench): shaft floor — light-shaft sand: a bright pale trench sand lit from the surface doors above, the pools of light drawn in the floor’s own art as pale glints standing in the tread where the shafts land (design: six light shafts slanting down from surface doors, each landing on a lit sand patch — every patch a way back up; art layer only). Route 124 Trench’s own floor — the brightest trench floor in Maris: warm and sunlit where Route 126 Trench’s door floor is volcanic grey lit by carried lights, and paler than the crossing’s own grey-wet trench sand above it.
